OL,3,ARace to update services' computer
OL,4,Asystems after cyber-security flaw found
OL,5,
OL,6,FOrganisations and businesses are still
OL,7,Fscrambling to update their systems
OL,8,Fafter cyber-security flaws were
OL,9,Frevealed in a widely-used programming
OL,10,Flanguage, PHP.
OL,12,FWebsites around the world were taken
OL,13,Foffline on Wednesday and Thursday after
OL,14,Fthe developers of PHP said "critical
OL,15,Fvulnerabilities" were found in the
OL,16,Fback-end language, used in web
OL,17,Fdevelopment for decades.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1792721905
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ARace to update services' computer
OL,4,Asystems after cyber-security flaw found
OL,5,
OL,6,FResearchers warned the "severe" flaws
OL,7,Fcould expose millions of sites using it
OL,8,Fto potential hacks if left unpatched -
OL,9,Fand the UK government was among those
OL,10,Fto take some sites offline as a
OL,11,Fprecaution.
OL,13,FThere have been no successful attacks
OL,14,Freported so far, but experts say any
OL,15,Fimpact may take time - even months - to
OL,16,Fbecome fully apparent.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
